{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2401 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "de9a29eb76035f1ce1c5e1a6aa40b0e2280ea31e9876980d9c966fbaad442317" :edb/db-before-t 2400 :edb/db-after-t 2401 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535713 50 #inst "2026-10-09T05:48:03.070Z" 13194139535713 true] [17592186161985 1020 #edb/ref 17592186362866 13194139535713 true] [17592186161986 1020 #edb/ref 17592186362859 13194139535713 true] [17592186162184 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535713 true] [17592186162184 1100 "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix above. Find its decomposition using Jordan blocks." 13194139535713 true] [17592186162184 1100 "$\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nConsider the matrix above. Find its decomposition using Jordan blocks." 13194139535713 false] [17592186162184 1145 "Our matrix can be represented as a single Jordan block:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]={J}_{3}(-2)\n$$" 13194139535713 true] [17592186162185 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535713 true] [17592186162185 1100 "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix above. Find its decomposition using Jordan blocks." 13194139535713 true] [17592186162185 1100 "$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nConsider the matrix above. Find its decomposition using Jordan blocks." 13194139535713 false] [17592186162185 1145 "Our matrix can be represented as the composition of two Jordan blocks (one $2\\times 2$ block and one $1\\times 1$ block), as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]={J}_{2}(1)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{1}(0)\n$$" 13194139535713 true] [17592186162187 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535713 true] [17592186162187 1100 "${J}_{2}(7)=$" 13194139535713 true] [17592186162187 1100 "What is $J_{2}(7)$?" 13194139535713 false] [17592186162187 1145 "Let's construct our matrix:\n\n- The index $2$ in ${J}_{2}(7)$ means that we have a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\n- The value $7$ in ${J}_{2}(7)$ means that we have $7$'s on the main diagonal.\n\n- Also, we must have $1$'s on the superdiagonal (the diagonal above the main one).\n\nGiven that all the other entries must be zero, our Jordan block is\n\n$$\n{J}_{2}(1)=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535713 true] [17592186362859 1017 #edb/ref 17592186362860 13194139535713 true] [17592186362859 1089 "q-108969" 13194139535713 true] [17592186362859 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535713 true] [17592186362859 1100 "${J}_{3}(-8)=$" 13194139535713 true] [17592186362859 1113 #uuid "8806f27c-bac9-5626-83fa-5aa4b2d96f89" 13194139535713 true] [17592186362859 1145 "Let's construct our matrix:\n\n- The index $3$ in ${J}_{3}(-8)$ means that we have a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n- The value $-8$ in ${J}_{3}(-8)$ means that we have $-8$'s on the main diagonal.\n\n- Also, we must have $1$'s on the superdiagonal (the diagonal above the main one).\n\nGiven that all the other entries must be zero, our Jordan block is\n\n$$\n{J}_{3}(-8)=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535713 true] [17592186362860 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362861 13194139535713 true] [17592186362860 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362862 13194139535713 true] [17592186362860 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362863 13194139535713 true] [17592186362860 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362864 13194139535713 true] [17592186362860 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362865 13194139535713 true] [17592186362860 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535713 true] [17592186362860 1041 "selection" 13194139535713 true] [17592186362860 1104 #edb/ref 17592186362864 13194139535713 true] [17592186362860 1110 #uuid "559dfb67-c3ea-5c90-a4b1-a8e2db4e31a2" 13194139535713 true] [17592186362861 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535713 true] [175